 Overlap expands heartbeat and persistence carriers uniquely, rejecting repeated complete pairs and duplicate heartbeat identities. Only containing operation intervals enter overlap; nested phase summaries do not inflate it or alter target samples. Current rehearsal verification and independent native proof require strict phase validation before acceptance.

 There are19 fixed names, at most19 summaries per observation, and a16KiB phase-summary validation bound. Runtime memory is one fixed-name recorder per active window plus completed carriers, independent of archive history. No new durable file or fsync is added. Phase bookkeeping, JSON serialization and extra bytes remain inside the existing actual time guards. Observer overhead is measured in preparation; this is observability, not a remedy for historical latency or evidence of long-run reliability.
+
+Active append observations use one eight-observation budget (1 ms waits, including
+post-validation observation) shared across a poll's read/publication seams and
+across an active checkpoint's retries. The existing both-advanced fixed timestamp
+pair remains valid. The additional split sequence permits one ctime-first epoch,
+then exactly one mtime catch-up to that epoch; larger size under the converged
+pair remains mandatory. Stable timestamps alone never establish an append.
+
+The resolver validates the entire captured interval by hash and pending read bytes
+by exact comparison. Observed source extent is distinct from captured cursor:
+unread tail is provisional and never included in a prefix hash or terminal cutoff.
+Source identity, unique live pathname, and archive metadata remain mandatory.
+Active checkpoints repeat the full prefix read after resolution; held source
+reads are unbuffered so a repeat cannot reuse stale Python reader bytes. Outgoing
+seal checks have no active-transition exception. Finish still requires an exact,
+fully consumed terminal source snapshot.
+
+Private sourceObservationFailure records carry the failing stage, compared stat
+tuples, captured/pending intervals, cursor and pre-transition observed extent.
+archivePublished/manifestPublished indicate publication by the failing append
+stage; prior captured bytes are always identified by capturedInterval, including
+at a checkpoint that performs no append publication itself. A collection row's
+pollComplete reports whether its poll returned. bytes counts completed polls;
+an incomplete poll can have already published provisional bytes, exposed by the
+failure record. Existing poll/receipt writes carry the bounded details; no new
+per-poll durable write is introduced. All work remains inside the actual guards.
